# Per-site collector settings. Copy to `.env` IN THIS DIRECTORY and edit:
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#   docker compose up -d --build
#
# Compose reads `.env` from the directory of the compose file automatically, so
# no flags and no long inline command. It is gitignored — the values differ per
# site and per machine, which is the point: the site id and the two serial paths
# end up recorded on the Pi they belong to instead of living in shell history.
#
# WHY THIS FILE AND configuration.env BOTH EXIST — they are not redundant, they
# feed two different mechanisms and are not interchangeable:
#
#   this .env          -> ${VAR} interpolation INSIDE compose.yaml. Compose
#                         substitutes these before it does anything, which is
#                         why `devices:` and the `:?` guards can use them.
#   configuration.env  -> `env_file:`, injected into the container's environment
#                         at run time. NOT visible to ${VAR} interpolation.
#
# So the MQTT passwords stay in configuration.env (the app reads them from its
# own environment) and never appear here. Putting a var in the wrong file fails
# quietly: interpolation yields an empty string.

# ── Required (the `:?` guards below refuse to start without them) ─────────────

# Which PBX site this collector is instrumenting. Selects the MQTT account
# (p1/p2, confined by the ACL to its own subtree), the password looked up as
# MQTT_PASSWORD_P1/P2, and the topic meshtastic-testbed/<site>/pbx.
COLLECTOR_SITE=p1

# The LiLyGO Meshtastic node's USB console (node-logd reads TX outcomes here).
# The nRF52840's J-Link VCOM (pbx-logd reads the PBX's own log here).
#
# Use /dev/serial/by-id paths, NOT /dev/ttyUSB0 — enumeration order changes
# across reboots and the failure is silent. Find them with:
#   ls -l /dev/serial/by-id/
# The LiLyGO shows up as usb-1a86_*, the nRF52840 as usb-SEGGER_J-Link*.
#
# Swapping these two is the easy mistake and it fails QUIETLY: both containers
# start clean and report nothing, because the two consoles share no grammar.
# Check lines_rejected on the first counter dump (~30 s) — if it climbs in step
# with lines_seen, the ports are crossed.
NODE_SERIAL_PORT=/dev/serial/by-id/usb-1a86_USB_Single_Serial_XXXXXXXX-if00
PBX_SERIAL_PORT=/dev/serial/by-id/usb-SEGGER_J-Link_XXXXXXXXX-if00

# Host running the gateway's Mosquitto broker.
#
# NOT localhost: the collector runs in its own compose project with its own
# network, so localhost is the container itself. Use the gateway host's address
# on the building network. If the broker happens to run on this same machine,
# 172.17.0.1 (the docker bridge gateway) reaches it.
BROKER_ADDRESS=192.168.1.10

# ── Optional (defaults in parentheses) ───────────────────────────────────────

# BROKER_PORT=1883
# PBX_COUNTERS_EVERY_SEC=30        # how often pbx-logd dumps its counters
# COLLECTOR_EXPIRY_SEC=120         # node-logd: age at which a pending TX is
#                                  # written off as unacked
